    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-match \"possible duplicate\" feature on `POST /api/owners`. A new owner that isn't a hard duplicate (telephone already in use) but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a *different* telephone is still created, and returned flagged.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **New OfficeFloor function** \u2014 `rest/function/owner/DetectPossibleDuplicate.java`: scans existing owners for one matching `lastName` (case-insensitive) + `postcode` with a different telephone; on a match sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf=<lowest matching id>`, otherwise `possibleDuplicate=false`. It runs before save (so `findAll()` sees only pre-existing owners), mirroring the existing `CountNamesakes` pattern.\n\n2. **Wiring** \u2014 `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`: inserted the `detectPossibleDuplicate` step between `flagBulkSignup` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance. This sits after the existing `rejectDuplicate` (hard-duplicate) check, so soft matches survive to be flagged.\n\n3. **Entity** \u2014 `model/Owner.java`: added persisted `possibleDuplicate` (Boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (Integer) columns with getters/setters, so the values are read back on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n4. **API schema** \u2014 `openapi.yml`: added `possibleDuplicate` and `possibleDuplicateOf` read-only properties to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries them and MapStruct auto-maps them by name (both the POST 201 body and the GET body go through `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`).\n\n5. **DB schema** \u2014 added the two columns to all four `db/*/schema.sql` files, and appended the two matching `NULL`s to hsqldb's positional `data.sql` seed inserts (the test profile is `hsqldb`; h2/postgres/mysql seeds use column-list inserts and needed no change).",
